# Offline oracle note — dfpt-spin-si (PW DFPT collinear spin, diamond Si)

## Intent

Pin Γ-point DFPT phonons for diamond Si with **collinear spin**
(`nspin=2`, multiplicity=1, LSDA) on the plane-wave method.

## Preferred oracle

CP2K Quickstep DFPT / `VIBRATIONAL_ANALYSIS` (or QE `ph.x`) on the same
cell with UKS / LSD and a comparable NC/GTH setup.

## Host status (2026-07-26)

No CP2K / QE module or binary on the pin host (`module avail cp2k` empty).
Sharp correctness pin is the **same-Hamiltonian central second difference
of the collinear-spin PW SCF total energy** (h = 0.03 Å) at identical
ecut/k/XC/UPF/spin — recorded in
`regressions/response/dfpt-spin-si/REFERENCE.md`.

## Twin settings (match regression)

| Item | Value |
| ---- | ----- |
| Cell | diamond Si, a = 5.43 Å, 2-atom fcc primitive |
| PP | `tests/data/pw/Si_lda_nc.upf` (in-tree NC ONCV) |
| XC | LSDA |
| Spin | collinear, multiplicity = 1 (M = 0) |
| ecut | 10 Ry |
| k-mesh | 2×2×2 MP |

When CP2K becomes available: record ω(Γ) [cm⁻¹], version, and wall for
fair ratio \(T_{\mathrm{atv}}/T_{\mathrm{cp2k}}\).
